--- A ui program's top level runs once as it starts, and reads its facts
--- as declared, and a derivation computed from them, in both modes. (The
--- compiled program had bound a fact as a Rust local only when a later
--- fact's default read it, so `log[count]` after the declarations did
--- not build; and a derivation read there was computed against the state
--- of a view that was not in scope.)
use ui

count = 21
twice = count * 2

derive data
    return count * 2

view render[]
    return p['`data` `twice`']

page['/', render]
log[count]
log[twice]
log[data]
log['`data` and `twice`']
